# Feature-Sliced Design

`apps/web` follows standard [Feature-Sliced Design](https://feature-sliced.design/ru/docs/get-started/overview).
Checked by two tools — keep both green:

- **Steiger** (`npm run lint:fsd` → `steiger ./src`, config `apps/web/steiger.config.ts`) — structure: public API,
  sidesteps, cross-slice imports, segment names, layer index files.
- **ESLint** `no-restricted-imports` (`apps/web/linter/rules/restricted-imports-rule.ts`) — layer direction,
  relative imports, public-API sidesteps, Spartan boundary.

## Layers

```
app → pages → widgets → features → entities → shared
```

A module may import only from layers **below** its own. Layers are created when needed (no empty `features/`).

| Layer | Holds | Slices? |
|---|---|---|
| `app/` | bootstrap config, providers, routes, root component | no — segments only |
| `pages/` | routed screens (`den`) | yes |
| `widgets/` | big self-contained UI blocks (`den-world`, `agent-panel`) | yes |
| `features/` | user interactions that bring value (toggle sound, switch skin) | yes |
| `entities/` | domain: `agent`, `skin`, `transcript` — stores, types, domain logic | yes |
| `shared/` | UI kit, collector socket, config, helpers — no domain knowledge | no — segments only |

**Pages first:** keep code inside the page (or the widget) that uses it; extract a widget / feature / entity when a
second consumer appears. Steiger's `fsd/insignificant-slice` (warning) points at slices used in one place only.

## Segments

The five standard segments. A custom segment is named by **purpose**, never `components`/`hooks`/`types`/`utils`.

- `ui/` — components (always `.ts` + `.html` + `.css`) and their formatters
- `model/` — signal stores, domain types, business logic, view-model derivation
- `api/` — talking to the outside world (collector socket, HTTP); internal to the slice
- `lib/` — helpers used inside the slice (formatters, pure utilities)
- `config/` — configuration and feature flags

Sub-folders inside a segment are fine for grouping (`entities/skin/model/cats/`).

## Public API

- Every **slice** has `index.ts`; so does every **shared segment** (`shared/ui/index.ts`, `shared/lib/index.ts`, ...).
  Segments inside a slice have their own `index.ts` too; the slice `index.ts` re-exports from them.
- **Layers have no `index.ts`** (no `src/entities/index.ts`) — layer barrels hide dependencies and create cycles.
- Explicit named re-exports only (`export { X } from '...'`, `export { type Y } from '...'`), never `export *`.
  Export only what consumers need.
- Index files use absolute `src/` paths.

```typescript
// src/entities/agent/index.ts
export { AgentStore, groupIntoRooms, type Room } from 'src/entities/agent/model';

// src/shared/ui/index.ts
export { DenPixelSprite, DenSheet, DenToggle } from 'src/shared/ui/...';
```

## Imports

| From → to | Form | Example |
|---|---|---|
| another layer's slice | `@layer/slice` | `import { AgentStore } from '@entities/agent';` |
| a shared segment | `@shared/segment` | `import { DenSheet } from '@shared/ui';` |
| inside the same slice (or inside `shared`) | absolute `src/...` | `import { DenCat } from 'src/widgets/den-world/ui/den-cat';` |
| workspace packages | package name | `import { reduceAgents } from '@agent-den/contracts';` |

Forbidden (ESLint + Steiger):

```typescript
import { AgentStore } from '@entities/agent/model/agent-store'; // ❌ sidesteps the public API
import { DenSheet } from '@shared/ui/sheet';                     // ❌ sidesteps the shared segment API
import { catsSkin } from '@entities/skin';                        // ❌ inside entities/agent: cross-slice import
import { DenWorld } from '@widgets/den-world';                    // ❌ inside entities: upper layer
import { DenCat } from './den-cat';                               // ❌ relative import
import { BrnSheet } from '@spartan-ng/brain/sheet';               // ❌ outside shared
```

**Cross-slice on the same layer** is not allowed. If two entities really must know each other, use FSD's
[`@x` notation](https://feature-sliced.design/docs/reference/public-api#public-api-for-cross-imports)
(`entities/agent/@x/skin.ts`) — don't add it without discussing first; usually the dependency belongs one layer up.

## UI kit boundary

- `@spartan-ng/*` is imported **only** inside `src/shared/**`.
- Every primitive is wrapped in `src/shared/ui/<name>/` (`den-*` selector, own styles) and exported from `@shared/ui`.
- If a wrapper is missing, add it to `shared/ui` first — upper layers never use Spartan directives directly.

## Creating new code

1. Pick the lowest layer where the code makes sense; start inside its consumer (pages first).
2. Create the slice folder (kebab-case) with segments.
3. Add `index.ts` to the slice and its segments; export only the public API.
4. Import other slices via `@layer/slice`, shared via `@shared/segment`, own files via `src/...`.
5. Run `npm run lint` (ESLint + Steiger).

## Current structure

```
src/
├── main.ts
├── styles.css
├── app/            index.ts, app.ts/.html, app.config.ts, app.routes.ts
├── pages/
│   └── den/        index.ts, ui/ (den-page)
├── widgets/
│   ├── den-world/  index.ts, ui/ (den-world, den-room, den-cat)
│   └── agent-panel/ index.ts, ui/ (agent-panel, transcript-feed), model/ (build-feed), lib/ (describe-agent)
├── entities/
│   ├── agent/      index.ts, model/ (agent-store, rooms)
│   ├── skin/       index.ts, model/ (skin, cats/…)
│   └── transcript/ index.ts, model/ (transcript-store)
└── shared/
    ├── api/        index.ts, collector-socket
    ├── config/     index.ts
    ├── lib/        index.ts, cn, hash, now
    └── ui/         index.ts, pixel-sprite/, sheet/, toggle/, search-field/
```
